export const metadata = { title: "Architecture \u2014 Athena docs" };

export default function Page() {
  return <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: "<h1 id=\"architecture\">Architecture</h1>\n<p>Athena turns a goal into a <strong>swarm</strong> and signs everything it does.</p>\n<pre><code>directive\n   \u2502\n   \u251c\u2500 tier router  (local embedding classifier, sub-millisecond, no model call)\n   \u2502     \u251c\u2500 fast   \u2192 one tool-free responder\n   \u2502     \u251c\u2500 medium \u2192 one capable tool-using agent\n   \u2502     \u2514\u2500 full   \u2192 the planned swarm \u2193\n   \u2502\n   \u251c\u2500 router      plans a team + a dependency graph\n   \u251c\u2500 specialists execute level-by-level, in parallel\n   \u251c\u2500 reflector   verifies each step, sends work back if needed\n   \u2514\u2500 lead        synthesizes the final answer\n             \u2193\n        every step Ed25519-signed \u2192 hash-chained ledger\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"the-tiers\">The tiers</h2>\n<p>Not every question deserves a committee. An embedding classifier (feature-hashing\nbag-of-words, nearest-exemplar \u2014 deterministic and model-free) picks the cheapest tier\nthat can do the job, and the <a href=\"/docs/self-evolution/\">self-evolving harness</a> improves that\nchoice from real outcomes.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-swarm\">The swarm</h2>\n<p>The <strong>router</strong> reads a one-line description of every specialist and composes a team plus\na dependency graph. Steps are topologically sorted into levels; everything in a level is\nindependent, so it runs concurrently. The <strong>reflector</strong> grades each step and can send it\nback for another attempt. A <strong>lead</strong> integrates the results into an answer to the\n<em>original</em> directive.</p>\n<p>The built-in roster (researcher, web, scientist, analyst, coder, engineer, tester,\nwriter) is data-driven \u2014 and you can add your own with <code>athena subagents add</code>, which the\nrouter will dispatch to like any other.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-ledger\">The ledger</h2>\n<p>Every agent is a cryptographic identity (Ed25519). Every reasoning step, tool call,\nskill synthesis, context compaction, and self-modification is signed by the acting agent\nand appended as a block whose hash chains to the previous one. Change any block and\nverification fails:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">athena verify   # \u2713 chain verified \u00b7 N signed blocks\n</code></pre>\n<p>The kernel is a native Rust crate (<code>native/athena_ledger</code>) for speed, and appends are\nthread-safe so parallel specialists can write concurrently.</p>\n<h2 id=\"skills-and-the-sandbox\">Skills and the sandbox</h2>\n<p>A <strong>skill</strong> is executable Python the swarm can call. When nothing fits, an agent emits\n<code>create_skill</code>; Athena synthesizes the code, runs a <strong>static capability check</strong> (rejecting\ncode that reaches for authority it wasn't granted), executes the auto-generated tests\n<strong>inside the sandbox</strong>, and only then injects it into the live run.</p>\n<p>Skills execute in a <strong>WebAssembly guest with no ambient authority</strong> \u2014 no syscalls by\ndefault \u2014 with fuel and wall-clock limits. A subprocess sandbox is the fallback backend.</p>\n<p>Skills have a lifecycle: <code>quarantined \u2192 promoted \u2192 deprecated</code>, driven by real usage.\nA failing skill is <strong>self-healed</strong> (repaired, re-tested, retried), and a proven one can be\npinned as a permanent tool.</p>\n<h2 id=\"memory\">Memory</h2>\n<p>Three layers, backed by AthenaDB:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>semantic</strong> \u2014 facts</li>\n<li><strong>episodic</strong> \u2014 what happened</li>\n<li><strong>procedural</strong> \u2014 skills, retrieved by similarity to the goal (pinned skills are always offered)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"context-management\">Context management</h2>\n<p>A long run's history is compacted under a fixed character budget: recent steps verbatim,\nolder ones as one-line digests, the deepest elided. Deterministic (no extra model call),\nand every compaction is signed.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-workspace\">The workspace</h2>\n<p>Opt-in real file access, confined to one directory with per-file and total size caps and\nguards against traversal, absolute paths, and symlinks. Tools: <code>write_file</code>, <code>read_file</code>,\n<code>list_files</code>, <code>make_dir</code>, <code>delete_path</code>, <code>edit_file</code>, <code>glob</code>, <code>grep</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"interfaces\">Interfaces</h2>\n<p>One FastAPI server exposes the HTTP API, streams runs over Server-Sent Events, and serves\nthe React dashboard. The <code>athena</code> CLI is a stdlib-only client over the same API, and\nthere's a native desktop app and messaging gateways.</p>\n<p>See also: <a href=\"/docs/security/\">security model</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/docs/self-evolution/\">self-evolving harness</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/docs/api/\">HTTP API</a></p>" }} />;
}
